    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Juan Muñoz-Guevara is a Lynwood City Council member, first elected in 2022. He works for UNITE HERE Local 11, a hospitality workers' union. He chairs the Metro Gateway Cities Service Council and serves on the Clean Power Alliance board and the Southern California Association of Governments Transportation Committee.",
        "cites": [1],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Juan Muñoz-Guevara is a Lynwood City Council member, first elected in 2022.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He works for UNITE HERE Local 11, a hospitality workers' union.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He chairs the Metro Gateway Cities Service Council and serves on the Clean Power Alliance board and the Southern California Association of Governments Transportation Committee.",
            "cites": [1]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "He supports making the city's fossil fuel divestment permanent and expanding the tree canopy. He says he helped Lynwood join the Clean Power Alliance, divest from fossil fuels, and secure nearly $15 million for parks and public investments, including turning a former gas station into a grocery store. He supports phasing out gas furnaces and water heaters to reduce smog-forming pollution.",
        "cites": [2, 3],
